body:
@AThousandShips Update on the reproduction state: This crash triggers exactly at the moment of quitting game.
Occured in Latest Stable 4.6
When transitioning away from the scene containing ~3,000+ instantiated objects, the engine attempts to free all these resources simultaneously. It appears Android 15's memory allocator aggressively frees up memory segments, destroying the mutexes before Godot's background cleanup/unreferencing threads finish executing their cycles. This causes `recursive_mutex::lock()` to call into a destroyed mutex during the exit/cleanup step, resulting in the hard `FORTIFY` SIGABRT.
